<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01DU">Proposition <span data-tag="01DU">4.5.1.5</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq }$ denote its core (Construction <a data-tag="01D0" href="/tag/01D0">4.4.3.1</a>). For every Kan complex $X$, composition with the inclusion map $\iota : \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq } \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ induces a bijection </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}} }( X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq } ) = \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}} }( X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq } ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}} }( X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}). \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="01DA" href="/tag/01DA">4.4.3.23</a>, postcomposition with $\iota $ induces an isomorphism of Kan complexes $\operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq } ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})^{\simeq }$. Proposition <a data-tag="01DU" href="/tag/01DU">4.5.1.5</a> follows by passing to connected components. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
